value problem\n![](images/8f/8fdedaad6e0d10a2bfab94f4266830a5efefbe2997d05455fecb35cbf7cefb43.svg)\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_1=2$ and $\\lambda_2=-3.$*" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)$ for the given system\n![](images/7a/7a07096a35f46528c18bdce5e711a5e813ac1923342e06cbff3f3c6b3215ae64.svg)\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n\\lambda_1= 2\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\lambda_2= -3.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For $\\lambda_1 =2,$ we get \n![](images/28/284acfc8cb4726bec4f4e805a8be0c037b38a0b9af287a27a4c7f5a2f1679d60.svg)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/b3/b33588ca4b487e1de13aac19bdfc5347751dbe95a9f93c27729d7da54ab02e06.svg)\n\n- For $\\lambda_2 =-3,$ we get \n![](images/1c/1c6b0e7303099895b50f884468ba6bfb7830ec88bbaea17dbc322a5a70eeea4c.svg)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/bb/bb4d152439d5a97dfda5196a24752e2048fb421a8cfac5c67ffbab512115d0c8.svg)\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2,$ we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution and use the initial values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+6{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}+6{c}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{c}_{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $c_2 = -1$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-1=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =6[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-216d1aeb-34d0-53e9-bbe2-39e35d3f0d63" :question/id #uuid "216d1aeb-34d0-53e9-bbe2-39e35d3f0d63" :question/math-academy-id "q-326296" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\ngiven that the general solution to our differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $-2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-5{c}_{1}=-5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n3\\cdot 1+{c}_{2}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-50a25668-c10b-5eab-bdcc-4ddc7f6b1b4e" "answer-field-dd206b91-8f38-5ab2-9e44-158195118e5a" "answer-field-7d4861c2-d3fe-5c16-bbc5-4dadf84b619c" "answer-field-5506a205-5b30-551f-b363-f141058018cc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-50a25668-c10b-5eab-bdcc-4ddc7f6b1b4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "50a25668-c10b-5eab-bdcc-4ddc7f6b1b4e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fc789ad9-fd8d-540d-b522-2e14081e3a89" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc789ad9-fd8d-540d-b522-2e14081e3a89"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc789ad9-fd8d-540d-b522-2e14081e3a89" :answer/id #uuid "fc789ad9-fd8d-540d-b522-2e14081e3a89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd206b91-8f38-5ab2-9e44-158195118e5a" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd206b91-8f38-5ab2-9e44-158195118e5a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-09520544-6bc1-51eb-8597-077df0f8f535" :answer-field/choices ["answer-09520544-6bc1-51eb-8597-077df0f8f535"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09520544-6bc1-51eb-8597-077df0f8f535" :answer/id #uuid "09520544-6bc1-51eb-8597-077df0f8f535" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d4861c2-d3fe-5c16-bbc5-4dadf84b619c