\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} \\\\ -{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=3 \\\\ -{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get\n\n$$\n4{c}_{2}=2\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=3\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e7da8384-bec0-52ca-95f9-6b880e18d11d" "answer-field-cf0e110a-54da-543d-aa0a-cb20cc674499" "answer-field-4265eaf3-4298-5be3-9a5f-defa76c03f8b" "answer-field-78faa26c-94b2-5ee2-86ab-c3fcb3b05b17"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e7da8384-bec0-52ca-95f9-6b880e18d11d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7da8384-bec0-52ca-95f9-6b880e18d11d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e5041c10-08ae-56e7-bc0e-86c30d564ece" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e5041c10-08ae-56e7-